{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 22, "model_name": "nvidia/llama-3.3-nemotron-super-49b-v1", "content": "i recently watched the movie \"the social network\" and here is my detailed review in all lower case as requested:\n\n**movie title:** the social network\n**director:** david fincher\n**release year:** 2010\n\n**storyline:**\nthe movie tells the story of how facebook came into existence. it focuses on the life of mark zuckerberg, a harvard university student who creates a website called \"thefacebook\" with the help of his roommates and fellow students, eduardo saverin, andrew mccollum, and chris hughes. as the website gains popularity, mark's relationships with his friends and family begin to deteriorate. the movie also explores the legal battles mark faces from his former friends and business partners.\n\n**acting:**\nthe entire cast delivered impressive performances. jesse eisenberg as mark zuckerberg was particularly convincing, portraying the character's introverted and slightly arrogant personality. andrew garfield as eduardo saverin brought depth to the film, highlighting the emotional struggle of being left out of the facebook success. justin timberlake as sean parker added a charming yet risky element to the story.\n\n**direction and cinematography:**\ndavid fincher's direction was impeccable, capturing the intense and competitive atmosphere of harvard university. the cinematography was sleek and modern, perfectly complementing the movie's theme of technology and innovation.\n\n**script:**\naaron sorkin's script was engaging and full of witty dialogue. the movie's narrative was well-structured, jumping back and forth between the creation of facebook and the legal depositions. the script successfully conveyed the moral ambiguities of the characters' actions.\n\n**music:**\nthe soundtrack by trent reznor and atticus ross was haunting and atmospheric, adding to the movie's tense moments.\n\n**overall impression:**\ni found \"the social network\" to be a compelling and thought-provoking movie. it not only tells the story of facebook's creation but also explores themes of friendship, betrayal, and the consequences of success. i would highly recommend this movie to anyone interested in technology, entrepreneurship, or just a well-crafted story.\n\n**rating:** 4.5/5\n\n**recommendation:**\nif you haven't seen \"the social network\" yet, i definitely recommend watching it. it's a great example of how a true story can be transformed into an engaging movie experience.", "logprobs": [{"token": "i", "logprob": -0.04083649069070816}, {"token": " recently", "logprob": -1.5719144344329834}, {"token": " watched", "logprob": -0.17987512052059174}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.4827228784561157}, {"token": " movie", "logprob": -0.0003182381624355912}, {"token": " \"", "logprob": -0.00011526874004630372}, {"token": "the", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": " network", "logprob": -2.861018856492592e-06}, {"token": "\"", "logprob": -0.003980927634984255}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.008736127987504005}, {"token": " here", "logprob": -0.09368687868118286}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.10174711793661118}, {"token": " my", "logprob": -0.00038044367101974785}, {"token": " detailed", "logprob": -1.549708758830093e-05}, {"token": " review", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.013284505344927311}, {"token": " all", "logprob": -0.001413061749190092}, {"token": " lower", "logprob": -0.012518989853560925}, {"token": " case", "logprob": -1.7881377516459906e-06}, {"token": " as", "logprob": -0.11507879197597504}, {"token": " requested", "logprob": -0.002476246329024434}, {"token": ":\n\n", "logprob": -0.011114589869976044}, {"token": "**", "logprob": -0.0007247682078741491}, {"token": "movie", "logprob": -0.0008457897347398102}, {"token": " title", "logprob": -0.03786616027355194}, {"token": ":**", "logprob": -0.003146